===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmɪksə(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-mixer.wav|Audio (Berkshire)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪksə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who, or a device that, [[mix]]es or merges things together.
#: {{hypo|en|cement mixer|concrete mixer}}
# One who mixes or [[socialize]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|url=https://classic.esquire.com/article/1936/2/1/the-crack-up|title=The Crack-Up|month=February|year=1936|accessdate=2020-11-30|author=F. Scott Fitzgerald|authorlink=F. Scott Fitzgerald|work=Esquire|passage=I had seen so many people all my life—I was an average '''mixer''', but more than average in a tendency to identify myself, my ideas, my destiny with those of all classes that I came in contact with.}}
#* {{RQ:Peake Gormenghast|passage=Bad '''mixer''' as he was, he preferred to be "out of it" in a crowd than out of it altogether.}}
# A [[machine]] outfitted with (typically [[blunt]]) [[blade]]s with which it [[mix]]es or [[beat]]s ingredients in a [[bowl]] below.
#: {{hypo|en|hand mixer|stand mixer|electric whisk}}
#: {{cot|en|blender|food processor}}
# A non-alcoholic drink (such as [[lemonade]], [[Coca-Cola]] or [[fruit juice]]) that is added to [[spirit]]s to make [[cocktail]]s.
#: {{ux|en|Do we have any '''mixers'''? I don't want to drink this vodka neat.}}
# {{lb|en|sound engineering}} A [[mixing console]].
# {{senseid|en|socialevent}}{{lb|en|US}} A dance or other social event meant to foster new acquaintances, as at the beginning of a school year.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Becky Hughes|title=The Hot New Thing in Dating? Actually Going on Dates.|work=The New York Times|date=2022-01-27|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/27/style/thursday-dating-app-mixers.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=To encourage those IRL meetings, Thursday hosts events in London and New York, the two cities where it is up and running; the '''mixer''' at Hair of the Dog was its eighth in this city and drew a crowd of about 450.}}
# Any of various [[social]] [[dance]]s involving frequent changes of [[partner]]s.
# A device for combining hot and cold water before it emerges from a single [[spout]] or [[shower head]].
# {{lb|en|electronics}} A [[nonlinear]] [[electrical circuit]] that creates new [[frequency|frequencies]] from two [[signal]]s applied to it.

